      "evidence": "tests/test_platform_module_identity.py (candidate.diff ~1379-1460): it does two things. It scans statically for `sys.modules[...] =` assignments. It also imports every test module in forward and reverse order and checks `identity_violations` on module namespaces. No test compares `sys.modules` before and after a test or module, for example by catching a `mock.patch.dict` stand-in that outlives its test. No test compares an isolated group run with an in-group run (spec scenario \"Group runs in isolation and in its group\"). The report format is `<owner>.<attribute> holds a substituted <name> instance`, which does name both the module and the test module as the scenario requires.",
      "id": "guard-does-not-check-runtime-sys-modules-leak",
